---
import DocLayout from '../../../layouts/DocLayout.astro';
---

<DocLayout title="Components" description="Farn component patterns — buttons, cards, forms, navigation, and more" section="components">
  <h1>Components</h1>
  <p>
    Farn is a token system, not a component library. This reference specifies what
    components should look like and how they should behave — using which tokens, with
    which states, following which accessibility rules. Implementation lives in your project.
  </p>
  <p>All components use semantic tokens only — never raw palette tokens. The surface declaration handles dark/light adaptation automatically.</p>

  <div class="comp-grid">
    <a href="/docs/components/buttons" class="comp-card">
      <h2 class="comp-card-title">Buttons &amp; Badges</h2>
      <p class="comp-card-desc">Five button variants, three sizes. Badge colour semantics — moss, grain, ember, heather, forest.</p>
      <span class="comp-card-cta">View spec →</span>
    </a>
    <a href="/docs/components/cards" class="comp-card">
      <h2 class="comp-card-title">Cards</h2>
      <p class="comp-card-desc">Flat inset style. Default, highlight-light, and highlight-dark variants. Grid sizing patterns.</p>
      <span class="comp-card-cta">View spec →</span>
    </a>
    <a href="/docs/components/forms" class="comp-card">
      <h2 class="comp-card-title">Forms &amp; Inputs</h2>
      <p class="comp-card-desc">Filled style inputs. Rest, hover, focus, error, and disabled states. Validation patterns.</p>
      <span class="comp-card-cta">View spec →</span>
    </a>
    <a href="/docs/components/navigation" class="comp-card">
      <h2 class="comp-card-title">Navigation</h2>
      <p class="comp-card-desc">Main nav bar, in-page tab navigation, focus styles, and surface section patterns.</p>
      <span class="comp-card-cta">View spec →</span>
    </a>
  </div>

  <h2>Token Usage Rules</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Components reference <code>--color-*</code> semantic tokens only — never <code>--fo1-fern</code> or other palette tokens directly.</li>
    <li>Hover and focus states use the provided semantic aliases: <code>--color-accent-hover</code>, <code>--color-bg-elevated</code>, etc.</li>
    <li>Surface declarations (<code>data-surface="dark"</code>, etc.) on parent elements re-scope all token values automatically — no conditional logic needed in component CSS.</li>
    <li>Bloom palette colours are reserved for semantic states (error, warning, success, annotation). Never use them decoratively.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Focus Styles</h2>
  <p>A single consistent focus ring across all interactive elements — defined once in <code>base.css</code>, applied everywhere via <code>:focus-visible</code>. Never remove focus styles.</p>
  <pre><code>:focus-visible &#123;
  outline: 2px solid var(--color-accent);
  outline-offset: 3px;
  border-radius: inherit;
&#125;

:focus:not(:focus-visible) &#123;
  outline: none;
&#125;</code></pre>
  <p><code>focus-visible</code> ensures the ring only appears for keyboard navigation — not on mouse click. <code>border-radius: inherit</code> follows the element's shape automatically.</p>

  <h2>Dark / Light Sections</h2>
  <p>Full-width page sections with explicit surface declarations. All child components inherit the correct tokens automatically — no extra markup needed.</p>
  <pre><code>&lt;section data-surface="light"&gt; &hellip; &lt;/section&gt;
&lt;section data-surface="dark"&gt; &hellip; &lt;/section&gt;
&lt;section data-surface="tinted"&gt; &hellip; &lt;/section&gt;</code></pre>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Surface</th><th>Background</th><th>Use</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>light</code></td><td><code>--bm2-parchment</code></td><td>Default. Most content sections.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>dark</code></td><td><code>--in0-void</code></td><td>Hero, feature callouts, closing CTAs.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>tinted</code></td><td><code>--bm1-linen</code></td><td>Subtle variation within a light page.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>Sections are flush — no gap between them. The background colour change is the visual separator. Page rhythm example: <strong>dark hero &rarr; light features &rarr; tinted aside &rarr; dark CTA</strong>.</p>
</DocLayout>

<style>
  .comp-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-md);
    margin: var(--space-xl) 0 var(--space-2xl);
    max-width: var(--width-prose);
  }
  .comp-card {
    background: var(--color-bg-elevated);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    padding: var(--space-lg);
    text-decoration: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-xs);
    transition: background-color 150ms ease, border-color 150ms ease;
  }
  .comp-card:hover {
    background: var(--color-bg-sunken);
    border-color: var(--color-accent);
  }
  .comp-card-title {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 16;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .comp-card-desc {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.55;
    margin: 0;
    max-width: none;
    flex: 1;
  }
  .comp-card-cta {
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    margin-top: var(--space-xs);
  }
</style>
